 "nota_seeds_compartilhados": "the 4 cells use the SAME grid of N=132 blocks (same assign_groups with grid_km=10) and the SAME 100 seeds (RandomState(20260927) generated a single time, reused in processar_celula for each city). The agreement between cells does not measure Monte Carlo error nor is it an independent replication; it is the SAME block permutation applied to 4 different geometries.",
 "errata": {
  "data": "2026-09-26",
  "motivo": "internal note (internal/note_26.md, block 1/5): the first round of classe_k_e_dist_borda.existe(gx,gy) computed ids=gx*max_y+gy WITHOUT checking 0<=gy<max_y (nor 0<=gx<max_x); nodes of the bottom row (gy=0) with dy<b 'found' block (gx-1,max_y-1) -- a GHOST NEIGHBOR -- inflating k(i) at 211,185 nodes per cell (fismat_k_corrigido_bauru.json: 124,618 true k=1 nodes became k=2 and k=0 nodes became k=1). This accounted for 69% of the excess at k=1 (0.0171 of 0.0246 absolute points). Fixed: existe() now checks the bounds in both directions (gx and gy) before testing whether the neighboring block exists.",
  "recomputado_nesta_rodada": true,
  "limitacao_declarada": "k(i) here counts only the 4 LATERAL neighbors (not diagonal ones); it is a proxy for m(i) of Proposition prop:inclusion of the internal note (which counts blocks of the 8-neighborhood by distance to the NODE, including diagonals). Hence the sandwich (ii) (k_te-1)_k/(N-1)_k <= p_i|te <= (N-1-k_tr)_k/(N-1)_k uses the lateral-only k(i) as an approximation of the exact geometric m(i); the remaining part of the excess at k=1/k=2 (face discretization and second-order effect of the validation neighbor) is quantified in fismat_k_corrigido_bauru.json / fismat_inclusao_decomp.json, not recomputed here for reasons of scope (it would require reclassifying per NODE, with diagonals, which changes the script beyond the requested correction).",
  "residual_nao_explicado_aprox": "~0.0075 of 0.0246 (31%) at k=1, see fismat_inclusao_decomp.json"
 },
